WEBVTT

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:06.910
A loaded truck and a tennis ball are both coming at you at 20 metres per

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:07.470
second.

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:11.030
Which one would you rather stop with your hands?

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:14.930
Two things make the truck harder to stop.

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:17.810
Pause and say what they are.

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:23.970
It's mass and how fast it's going.

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:26.590
Today we turn hard to stop into a number.

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:28.710
It's called momentum.

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:32.850
Learn this word for word.

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:35.550
It comes straight from SAGS.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:40.690
Linear momentum is the product of the mass and velocity of the object.

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:45.370
P equals m times v or m v.

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:46.850
Mass is in kilograms.

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:49.830
Velocity is in metres per second.

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:54.370
So the unit is the kilogram metre per second.

00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:58.930
Same ball, same speed.

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:00.990
One goes east, one goes west.

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:02.990
Do they have the same momentum?

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:04.890
Pause and decide.

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:07.870
No.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:09.210
Momentum is a vector.

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:10.730
Take east as positive.

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:17.230
The ball going east has momentum of positive, 6,24 kilograms, metres per second.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:20.490
The ball going west has negative, 6,24.

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:23.370
Same size, opposite signs.

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:27.030
The signs matter for the rest of this module.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:41.270
Worked example 7.1, a cricket ball has a mass of 156 grams, it's bowled at

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:44.810
135 kilometres an hour due west.

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:48.570
First I choose east as positive.

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:59.610
Now I convert the mass 156 grams divided by 1000, that's 0,156 kilograms.

00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:11.160
Now the speed, 135 divided by 3,6, that's 37,5 metres per second.

00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:17.220
It's going west, so the velocity is negative 37,5.

00:02:18.350 --> 00:02:27.820
P equals m v or m times v, 0,156 times negative 37,5.

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:31.680
That gives negative 5,85.

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:38.260
So the momentum is 5,85 kilogram metres per second west.

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:40.500
That's four marks.

00:02:41.030 --> 00:02:45.680
One for the conversion, one for the formula, one for the substitution and

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:48.340
one for the answer with its direction.

00:02:49.370 --> 00:02:49.600
Pause.

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:52.800
Why must the answer say West?

00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:58.840
Because momentum is a vector.

00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:02.700
A number without a direction loses the mark.

00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:05.160
Your turn.

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:09.250
A cyclist and her bicycle have a mass of 65 kilograms.

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:12.690
She rides north at 8,5 metres per second.

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:15.530
Pause and work out her momentum.

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:24.930
552,5 kilograms metres per second north.

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:26.490
Did you remember north?

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:32.330
When a net force acts, the momentum changes.

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:35.770
Change in momentum is final minus initial.

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:38.330
Always final minus initial.

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:40.450
Most marks are lost in two places.

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:41.490
Step 2.

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:43.030
Take your positive direction.

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:43.910
Step 3.

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:46.390
Give both velocities a sign.

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:48.830
Predict.

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:51.070
A ball hits a wall and stops.

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:54.790
The same ball hits the wall and bounces back at the same speed.

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:57.410
Which one has the bigger change in momentum?

00:03:57.940 --> 00:03:59.130
Pause and decide.

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:05.590
Look at the change in momentum under the graph.

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:11.250
For the stop it's negative 2 kilogram metres per second.

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:13.230
For the bounce it's negative 4.

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:14.890
Bouncing back doubles it.

00:04:15.140 --> 00:04:18.490
The ball has to stop and then go the other way.

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:20.930
Worked example

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:21.870
7,2.

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:24.850
A ball has a mass of 200 grams.

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:28.430
It moves to the right at 12 metres per second.

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:33.410
A bat sends it back to the left at 8 metres per second.

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:35.750
Take right as positive.

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:40.970
So u is positive 12 and v is negative 8.

00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:45.490
And 200 grams is 0,2 kilograms.

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:51.470
Delta p equals m times v take away u.

00:04:51.820 --> 00:04:55.530
That's 0,2 times negative 8 take away 12.

00:04:56.360 --> 00:04:59.250
Negative 8 take away 12, that's negative 20.

00:04:59.780 --> 00:05:03.590
Then 0,2 times negative 20, that's negative 4.

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:09.390
So the change in momentum is 4 kilograms metres per second to the left.

00:05:09.960 --> 00:05:15.070
A learner wrote 0,2 times 8 take away 12.

00:05:15.420 --> 00:05:16.970
She got negative 0,8.

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:17.690
Pause.

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:18.730
What went wrong?

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:24.370
She dropped the negative sign on the 8.

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:26.590
The velocity didn't change by 4.

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:29.010
It went from positive 12 to negative 8.

00:05:29.260 --> 00:05:30.690
That's a change of 20.

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:32.810
Your turn.

00:05:33.450 --> 00:05:36.240
A soccer ball has a mass of 0,43 kilograms.

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:39.700
It moves west at 10 metres per second.

00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:43.520
It's headed back east at 14 metres per second.

00:05:43.850 --> 00:05:45.140
Take east as positive.

00:05:45.650 --> 00:05:47.040
Pause and work it out.

00:05:50.290 --> 00:05:54.960
0,43 times 14 take away negative 10.

00:05:55.150 --> 00:05:58.560
That's 0,43 times 24.

00:05:59.090 --> 00:06:04.600
So the change in momentum is 10,32 kilograms metres per second east.

00:06:07.110 --> 00:06:08.460
Newton's second law.

00:06:08.750 --> 00:06:14.180
In SAGS words, the net force acting on an object is equal to the rate of

00:06:14.190 --> 00:06:15.620
change of momentum.

00:06:16.510 --> 00:06:20.920
So, F net equals delta p divided by delta t.

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:29.010
Same ball same bat the contact time is 0,02 seconds negative 4 divided by

00:06:29.020 --> 00:06:35.350
0,02 that's negative 200 so the average net force is 200 newtons to the

00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:42.530
left pause the ball was moving right why is the force on it to the left

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:50.890
the force points the same way as a change in momentum it's the force that

00:06:50.900 --> 00:06:52.310
turns the ball around

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:56.830
Impulse is the product of the net force and the contact time.

00:06:57.560 --> 00:06:59.710
Impulse equals the change in momentum.

00:07:00.880 --> 00:07:05.110
So newton seconds and kilogram metres per second are the same unit.

00:07:05.680 --> 00:07:08.730
This orange rectangle is the impulse.

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:10.390
Force times time.

00:07:11.220 --> 00:07:14.610
Right now the impulse is negative 2 newton seconds.

00:07:15.220 --> 00:07:17.330
The force is negative 10 newtons.

00:07:17.920 --> 00:07:20.470
I'm going to make the stopping time four times longer.

00:07:20.760 --> 00:07:22.050
What happens to the force?

00:07:22.840 --> 00:07:23.650
Pause and predict.

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:34.490
The area stays the same because it's the same stop the size of the force

00:07:34.500 --> 00:07:40.390
drops to a quarter two comma five newtons keep this picture in mind it's

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:41.890
the whole of the next part

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:43.930
Your turn.

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:48.300
A stationary ball has a mass of 0,25 kilograms.

00:07:49.310 --> 00:07:52.920
An average net force of 40 newtons acts on it to the left.

00:07:53.310 --> 00:07:55.800
It acts for 0,015 seconds.

00:07:56.790 --> 00:07:59.680
Find the change in momentum then the final velocity.

00:08:00.190 --> 00:08:01.380
Pause and work it out.

00:08:05.410 --> 00:08:07.700
Take right as positive.

00:08:08.390 --> 00:08:10.300
So the force is negative 40.

00:08:10.990 --> 00:08:14.120
Negative 40 times 0,015.

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:16.360
That's negative 0,6.

00:08:16.950 --> 00:08:22.500
So the change in momentum is 0,6 kilogram metres per second to the left.

00:08:23.610 --> 00:08:24.900
It started at rest.

00:08:25.870 --> 00:08:29.940
So v is negative 0,6 divided by 0,25.

00:08:29.950 --> 00:08:32.480
That's negative 2,4.

00:08:32.770 --> 00:08:36.880
So the final velocity is 2,4 metres per second to the left.

00:08:40.360 --> 00:08:42.910
Same ball, same speed, same stop.

00:08:43.400 --> 00:08:45.770
So the same change in momentum.

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:50.310
The only thing you can change is the time it takes to stop.

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:56.290
This explanation is worth 3 marks nearly every paper.

00:08:56.600 --> 00:08:58.190
Say 3 things in this order.

00:08:58.480 --> 00:08:58.690
1.

00:08:59.020 --> 00:09:00.970
The change in momentum is the same.

00:09:01.300 --> 00:09:01.870
2.

00:09:02.220 --> 00:09:03.770
The stopping time increases.

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:05.770
Name what does it.

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:06.950
3.

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:10.850
F net is delta p divided by delta t.

00:09:11.540 --> 00:09:13.490
So the average net force decreases.

00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:19.540
Here's the trap.

00:09:19.970 --> 00:09:24.100
Never say the airbag makes the change in momentum smaller.

00:09:25.090 --> 00:09:28.580
The November revision memo says it word for word.

00:09:29.030 --> 00:09:33.220
Do not say that the change in momentum becomes smaller.

00:09:34.710 --> 00:09:36.140
Your turn.

00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:40.400
A goalkeeper pulls her hands back as she catches a hard shot.

00:09:41.070 --> 00:09:43.740
Pause and write the three mark explanation.

00:09:47.430 --> 00:09:51.680
Same delta p, longer stopping time so a smaller average force.

00:09:51.970 --> 00:09:52.520
Three ticks.

00:09:54.110 --> 00:09:56.420
That's momentum and impulse.

00:09:56.930 --> 00:10:02.460
Next in the app is see it happen, that's the impulse lab on its own, then

00:10:02.470 --> 00:10:05.020
train, then check with no help.
